  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "kind": "prep",
      "primary_message": "Zest and juice the limes. Shuck the corn, then cut off the kernels with a knife. Cut the red pepper into 1/2-inch squares. Finely mince the jalapeño pepper. Trim the ends of the green beans, then cut them into 1-inch lengths. Cut the radishes into bite-sized pieces. Peel and cut the jicama into 3/4-inch dice. Pick the cilantro leaves from the stems and roughly chop them.",
      "secondary_message": "2 limes\n1 ¾ cups corn\n1 red pepper\n1 jalapeño pepper\n113 g green beans\n1 bunch radishes\n1 bulb jicama\n½ cup fresh cilantro leaves"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "Combine lime juice, lime zest, and honey in a medium bowl. Whisking constantly, slowly drizzle in olive oil. Season to taste with salt and pepper. Set aside.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Heat vegetable oil in a large nonstick or cast iron skillet over high heat until shimmering. Add corn, shake once to distribute, and cook without moving until darkly charred on first side, about 3 minutes. Toss and flip corn and repeat until corn is covered in dark spots, about 8 minutes total. Add bell pepper, jalapeño, and scallion whites. Cook, tossing frequently, until softened, about 2 minutes. Season to taste with salt and pepper. Transfer to a large bowl and allow to cool for a few minutes.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "Add green beans to boiling water and cook just until tender-crisp, about 3 minutes. Drain beans and run under cold running water until cool. Add beans to bowl with corn. Add radishes, jicama, white onion, cilantro, scallion greens, and dressing and toss to combine. Season to taste with salt and pepper. Serve.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
